WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.420
Mice that lack TRPM8, the cold and menthol receptor, were trained for ten days to

2
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.880
report warming of the forepaw.

3
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.560
They completely failed.

4
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.060
That sounds backwards.

5
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.600
A cold receptor should matter for cold.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.780
So why would a mouse without it miss warmth?

7
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:24.813
Here is the task. A head-fixed mouse is trained to report a temperature step on its

8
00:00:24.813 --> 00:00:31.433
forepaw. A Peltier surface, 8 by 8 mm, holds 32 °C, then steps.

9
00:00:32.253 --> 00:00:34.773
Trained mice reported a warming step of 1 °C.

10
00:00:35.313 --> 00:00:36.693
The mouse licks to report it.

11
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:42.337
Alongside the behaviour, the group recorded single fibres from forepaw skin, kept

12
00:00:42.337 --> 00:00:44.677
alive outside the animal with its nerve attached.

13
00:00:45.457 --> 00:00:46.917
This is a skin-nerve preparation.

14
00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:48.817
Each tick is one spike.

15
00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:51.457
They warmed the skin at 1 °C per second.

16
00:00:52.077 --> 00:00:57.277
One population, the polymodal C fibres, increased its firing as the skin warmed.

17
00:00:57.277 --> 00:00:59.057
Warming excites them.

18
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.740
A second population answered the opposite way.

19
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.580
These are cool-sensitive C fibres, about 19% % of the thermosensitive fibres

20
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:16.260
recorded. In a bath at 27 °C, they fired all the time, between 0.2 and 6 Hz.

21
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.660
Warming reduced that ongoing rate.

22
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:24.840
The group used 27 °C because thermal imaging showed awake forepaw skin at 26 to 28

23
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.340
At the usual 32 °C bath, this population had not been seen.

24
00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.990
Temperature is not read off one channel at a time.

25
00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.250
Warmth has two signals at once.

26
00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.790
Some fibres speed up.

27
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.550
Cool fibres slow down.

28
00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:44.470
Without TRPM8, the cool fibres lose their ongoing firing, and one part of the warmth

29
00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.810
signal is gone. Write that as reduced cool input.

30
00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:52.770
Here, no central circuit that flips the sign of the cool signal has been identified.

31
00:01:53.883 --> 00:01:54.943
Remember the bath.

32
00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:58.923
A signal that looks absent at one baseline may be there at another.

33
00:01:59.643 --> 00:02:03.423
The resting condition is part of the stimulus, not a neutral background.

34
00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:07.883
In the mouse forepaw, warmth is read from excitation and from silence.
